# Line-ending policy.
#
# This repository is developed on Windows and built on Linux. Shell scripts
# are the one file type where that combination actually breaks: a CRLF bash
# script fails on Linux/macOS with `bad interpreter` or `$'\r': command not
# found`, and the failure looks like a broken script rather than a broken
# checkout.
#
# Only *.sh is pinned. Everything else keeps the repository's existing
# behaviour, so this file cannot create a mass re-normalization diff.
*.sh text eol=lf
